@startuml Arc and Linear Interpolation — Current Architecture
title Arc and Linear Interpolation Flow (scurve_motion, March 2026)
' gcode_parser.c dispatches G-code events inline to motion_bridge.c.
' motion_bridge.c owns the arc state machine (incremental chord generator).
' trajectory.c holds the 64-slot S-curve planner with 3-pass lookahead.
' interpolator.c is the DDS step generator fed by the trajectory ring.
' TIMER_4_ISR executes Bresenham + velocity profile at IPL6.
!theme blueprint

participant "gcode_parser.c\n(Inline Dispatch)" as PARSER
participant "motion_bridge.c\n(Arc State Machine)" as BRIDGE
participant "kinematics.c\n(Coord Transform)" as KIN
participant "trajectory.c\n(S-curve Planner\n64-slot Ring)" as TRAJ
participant "interpolator.c\n(DDS Generator)" as INTERP
participant "TIMER_4_ISR\n(Bresenham + Velocity\nIPL6 Shadow Regs)" as ISR
participant "Step GPIO\n(Harmony Macros)" as GPIO

== Linear Move (G0 / G1) ==
PARSER -> BRIDGE : LINEAR_MOVE event {x,y,z,a, feedrate, is_rapid}
BRIDGE -> KIN : Work-space pos → machine-space pos\n  (WCS offset G54–G59 + G92 + TLO G43/G43.1/G49)
KIN -> BRIDGE : Machine CoordinatePoint
BRIDGE -> TRAJ : TRAJECTORY_AddMove(start_mach, end_mach, feedrate)
TRAJ -> TRAJ : compute unit_vec[], normalise\n  limit_acceleration_by_axis()  — slowest limiting axis\n  limit_rate_by_axis()          — slowest limiting axis
TRAJ -> TRAJ : junction speed (centripetal approximation, no trig):\n  cos_theta = -dot(prev_unit_vec, curr_unit_vec)\n  sin_half  = sqrt(0.5 * (1 - cos_theta))\n  v²_junc   = accel × junction_dev × sin_half / (1 - sin_half)
TRAJ -> TRAJ : Enqueue MotionSegment
TRAJ -> TRAJ : MOTION_PlannerRecalculate() (GRBL-exact 3-pass):\n  1. Reverse pass — cap entry_speed_sqr by decel constraints\n  2. Forward pass — cap entry_speed_sqr by accel constraints\n  3. Trapezoid pass — write to every buffered segment:\n       initial_rate, nominal_rate, final_rate,\n       accelerate_until, decelerate_after
note right of TRAJ
  PlannerRecalculate runs after EVERY enqueue.
  All buffered segments are re-optimised as a unit
  (look-ahead window = full 64-slot ring).
end note
PARSER -> PARSER : Send "ok" — or defer if traj queue ≥ HIGH_WATER (48)

== Arc Move (G2 / G3) — Incremental Chord Generator in motion_bridge.c ==
PARSER -> BRIDGE : ARC_MOVE event {G2/G3, end, I/J/K, feedrate, plane}
BRIDGE -> BRIDGE : Validate arc: |r_start − r_end| < $13\n  ALARM:5 if radius mismatch
BRIDGE -> BRIDGE : Compute:\n  centre (cx, cy) from I, J (always incremental)\n  start_angle = atan2(start.y−cy, start.x−cx)\n  end_angle   = atan2(end.y−cy,   end.x−cx)\n  total_angle (wrap-around for CW/CCW direction)\n  arc_length  = radius × |total_angle|\n  segments    = ceil(arc_length / $12 chord_deviation)
BRIDGE -> BRIDGE : armArcState = ARC_ACTIVE\n  store: centre, radius, theta=start_angle, thetaEnd,\n         thetaIncrement=total_angle/segments, arcEnd, plane
PARSER -> PARSER : "ok" deferred until arc command accepted (flow controlled)

loop One chord per APP_Tasks() iteration — non-blocking
  alt Trajectory queue not full
    BRIDGE -> BRIDGE : theta += thetaIncrement
    alt Not last segment
      BRIDGE -> BRIDGE : next.x = cx + r·cos(theta)\n  next.y = cy + r·sin(theta)\n  next.z = linear interp to arcEnd.z\n  next.a = linear interp to arcEnd.a
    else Last segment
      BRIDGE -> BRIDGE : next = arcEnd  (exact target — no accumulated error)
      BRIDGE -> BRIDGE : armArcState = ARC_IDLE
    end
    BRIDGE -> KIN : Work → machine coord transform for arc point
    KIN -> BRIDGE : machine-space point
    BRIDGE -> TRAJ : TRAJECTORY_AddMove(arcCurrent_mach, next_mach, feedrate)
    TRAJ -> TRAJ : Enqueue + MOTION_PlannerRecalculate()
    note right of TRAJ
      Junction speed between consecutive arc chords
      computed automatically by the planner.
      Smooth speed maintained throughout arc.
    end note
    BRIDGE -> BRIDGE : arcCurrent = next
  else Queue full (backpressure)
    BRIDGE -> BRIDGE : service_realtime_byte() — service pending '?' status
    note right of BRIDGE
      '?' status replies answered during backpressure.
      G-code bytes safe in push-back slot.
      Retry next APP_Tasks() iteration.
    end note
  end
end

== DDS Segment Load (interpolator.c, main loop) ==
INTERP -> INTERP : trajectory ring non-empty + currentSegment == NULL?\n  → pull next MotionSegment, load ISR statics:\n    delta[], abs_delta[], error[], direction_bits,\n    initial_rate, accelerate_until, decelerate_after
INTERP -> GPIO : DirX/Y/Z/A_Set/Clear (direction stable BEFORE first STEP)
INTERP -> ISR : TMR4_Start() — step pulses begin

== Per-Step Cycle (TIMER_4_InterruptHandler, IPL6) ==
activate ISR
ISR -> GPIO : OC1 dual-compare hardware auto-toggles dominant-axis STEP HIGH\n  (silicon — zero CPU involvement for rising edge)
ISR -> ISR : Guard: seg = currentSegment; return if NULL
ISR -> GPIO : switch(dominant_axis) → Harmony #define → single LATxSET
ISR -> ISR : AXIS_IncrementSteps / AXIS_DecrementSteps (always_inline)
loop Bresenham subordinate axes (0–3, bounded)
  ISR -> ISR : error[axis] += abs_delta[axis]
  alt error >= dominant_delta
    ISR -> GPIO : step subordinate axis → single LATxSET
    ISR -> ISR : error[axis] -= dominant_delta; update position counter
  end
end
ISR -> ISR : Velocity profile (integer only, no float, no division):\n  ACCEL  (sc < accelerate_until)  → step_interval -= rate_delta\n  DECEL  (sc >= decelerate_after) → step_interval += decel_rate_delta\n  CRUISE → unchanged
ISR -> ISR : PR4 = step_interval  (direct SFR, min clamp 7 ticks @ 781.25 kHz)
ISR -> ISR : steps_completed++\n  if complete: T4CONCLR inside ISR (stop timer mid-ISR)\n               motionSegmentCompleted = true; return
deactivate ISR

note over PARSER, GPIO
  Pulse width: ~2.56 µs (TMR5 one-shot). All four step pins cleared
  unconditionally by TMR5 callback. DRV8825 min: 1 µs; TMC5160 min: 100 ns.
end note

@enduml

package "G-code Parser" {
    [GCODE Event\nGenerator] as GCODE
    note right of GCODE
        Events:
        - LINEAR_MOVE (G1)
        - ARC_MOVE (G2/G3)
        - Modal params (F/S/T)
    end note
}

package "Application Layer (app.c)" {
    rectangle "APP_Tasks State Machine" {
        state "APP_IDLE" as IDLE {
            state "Process G-code\nEvents" as PROC
            state "Arc Generator\n(Incremental)" as ARC_GEN
            state "Motion Phase\nExecution" as PHASE
        }
    }
    
    [Arc State Machine] as ARC_SM
    note right of ARC_SM
        ARC_GEN_IDLE
        ARC_GEN_ACTIVE
        
        Generates ONE segment
        per iteration when:
        - arcGenState == ACTIVE
        - motionQueue has space
    end note
}

package "Kinematics Module (kinematics.c)" {
    [KINEMATICS_LinearMove] as LINEAR
    note right of LINEAR
        Converts geometric move
        to MotionSegment:
        - Bresenham deltas
        - Velocity profiling
        - Acceleration planning
        - Step counts
    end note
}

package "Motion Queue (APP_DATA)" {
    database "Motion Segment\nQueue [16]" as QUEUE {
        [MotionSegment 0]
        [MotionSegment 1]
        [MotionSegment ...]
        [MotionSegment 15]
    }
}

package "Motion Controller (motion.c)" {
    [MOTION_Tasks\nSegment Queue] as MOTION
    note right of MOTION
        Dequeues segments, calls
        STEPPER_LoadSegment().
        Polls steps_completed for
        segment completion.
    end note
}

' Linear Move Flow
GCODE -down-> PROC : LINEAR_MOVE\nevent
PROC -down-> LINEAR : CoordinatePoint\nstart, end,\nfeedrate
LINEAR -down-> QUEUE : MotionSegment\n(ready to execute)

' Arc Move Flow - Initial Setup
GCODE -down-> PROC : ARC_MOVE\nevent (G2/G3)
PROC -right-> ARC_SM : Initialize arc:\n- Calculate radius\n- Verify tolerance\n- Compute angles\n- Set segment count

' Arc Generation Loop
ARC_SM -down-> ARC_GEN : arcGenState =\nACTIVE
ARC_GEN -down-> LINEAR : One segment:\ntheta += increment\nsin/cos point
note on link
    Incremental Generation:
    • Non-blocking (50-100μs)
    • One segment per iteration
    • FPU sin/cos for arc point
    • Linear Z/A interpolation
end note

' Motion Execution
QUEUE -down-> MOTION : Pop segment\nfrom queue
MOTION -down-> [TIMER_4_ISR\nTMR4/TMR5\n(Single ISR)] : Step pulses\n(period-based timing)

' Arc Completion
ARC_GEN -right-> ARC_SM : Last segment?\narcGenState = IDLE
note on link
    Exact end point:
    Final segment uses
    target coordinates
    (no accumulated error)
end note

' Annotations
note bottom of QUEUE
    **Flow Control:**
    Queue fills faster than it drains
    → Smooth continuous motion
    → Never runs empty during arc
    
    **Self-Regulating:**
    Arc generator checks space
    before adding segment
end note

note bottom of LINEAR
    **Physics Calculations:**
    - Distance (Pythagorean)
    - Steps per mm (from settings)
    - Max velocity (feedrate)
    - Acceleration profile
    - Bresenham error terms
end note

' Legend
legend bottom right
    **Arc Interpolation Algorithm:**
    1. Validate radius: |r_start - r_end| < 0.005mm
    2. Calculate angles: start_angle, end_angle
    3. Compute arc_length = radius × total_angle
    4. Segment count = arc_length / mm_per_arc_segment
    5. Increment theta each iteration
    6. Generate point: (cx + r×cos(θ), cy + r×sin(θ))
    7. Call KINEMATICS_LinearMove() for segment
    8. Repeat until theta reaches end_angle
    
    **Key Features:**
    • GRBL v1.1 compatible arc math
    • G2 (CW) and G3 (CCW) support
    • Helical motion (linear Z/A)
    • Plane selection (G17/G18/G19)
    • FPU-accelerated (sin/cos)
end legend

@enduml
